From afbc7685f8578c65ea11e5940b21ae8a5623de5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:17:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Install, renew and remove apps on the iPhone for Cartouche

Cartouche installs an IPA as an app of its own on this iPhone through
the SideStore built into it, lists those apps, renews them and
uninstalls them, on its own screens (decision 142). SideStore gets three
actions for it, headless, which Cartouche runs through LiveContainer's
SideStoreSupport in LiveProcess as it runs Refresh All Apps:
CartoucheInstallAppIntent, CartoucheRefreshAppsIntent and
CartoucheRemoveAppIntent. Each takes its request from the app group
(CartoucheAppsRequest), where Cartouche also keeps the list of the apps
it installed (CartoucheInstalledApps), which Refresh All Apps renews
with Cartouche (patch 0017).

The install refuses, before anything goes to Apple, an app this
database already holds that is not on the list, another store's, and
an install that would pass the three active apps of a free Apple ID.
The removal deletes the app from the iPhone, or clears its record alone
when the iPhone has no such app any more. Refresh All Apps notes the
apps that failed in its outcome (CartoucheOutcome, patch 0014), for
Cartouche to show under each; CartoucheOutcome tells the refusals apart
by their kind, as the sign-in's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
